{"name":"Fire Ant","hex":"#be6400","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fire ant","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several red or yellow ants that can inflict a harsh sting.\nSolenopsis spp. (tropical fire ants)\nOecophylla spp. (weaver ants), of Southeast Asia\nSolenopsis invicta (red imported fire ant)\nWasmannia auropunctata (electric ant, little fire ant).","Solenopsis spp. (tropical fire ants)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fire_ant"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fire ant","blocks":[{"text":"Fire ants are several species of ants in the genus Solenopsis, which includes over 200 species. Solenopsis are stinging ants, and most of their common names reflect this, for example, ginger ants and tropical fire ants. Many of the names shared by this genus are often used interchangeably to refer to other species of ant, such as the term red ant, mostly because of their similar coloration despite not being in the genus Solenopsis. Both Myrmica rubra and Pogonomyrmex barbatus are common examples of non-Solenopsis ants being termed red ants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Fire_ants.jpg/330px-Fire_ants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_ant","wikidata":"Q1075697"},{"title":"Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Fire is the rapid oxidation of a fuel in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.\nFlames, the most visible portion of the fire, are produced in the combustion reaction when the fuel reaches its ignition point temperature. Flames from hydrocarbon fuels consist primarily of carbon dioxide, water vapor, oxygen, and nitrogen. If hot enough, the gases may become ionized to produce plasma. The color and intensity of the flame depend on the type of fuel and composition of the surrounding gases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Large_bonfire.jpg/330px-Large_bonfire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire","wikidata":"Q3196"},{"title":"Ant","blocks":[{"text":"Ants are eusocial insects of the family Formicidae and, along with the related wasps and bees, belong to the order Hymenoptera. Ants evolved from vespoid wasp ancestors in the Cretaceous period. More than 13,800 of an estimated total of 22,000 species have been described. They are easily identified by their geniculate (elbowed) antennae and the distinctive node-like structure that forms their slender waists."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Red_Ant_-_March_2025.jpg/330px-Red_Ant_-_March_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ant","wikidata":"Q7386"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/CSIRO_ScienceImage_11133_Tropical_fire_ant.jpg/500px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_11133_Tropical_fire_ant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/CSIRO_ScienceImage_11133_Tropical_fire_ant.jpg/1280px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_11133_Tropical_fire_ant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/CSIRO_ScienceImage_11133_Tropical_fire_ant.jpg/500px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_11133_Tropical_fire_ant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail of the head (Solenopsis geminata)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACSIRO_ScienceImage_11133_Tropical_fire_ant.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Fire_ant_queens_3589.jpg/500px-Fire_ant_queens_3589.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Fire_ant_queens_3589.jpg/1280px-Fire_ant_queens_3589.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Fire_ant_queens_3589.jpg/500px-Fire_ant_queens_3589.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Solenopsis winged reproductive females, queens and workers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFire_ant_queens_3589.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Solenopsis.jpg/500px-Solenopsis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Solenopsis.jpg/1280px-Solenopsis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Solenopsis.jpg/500px-Solenopsis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A fire ant worker (bottom), queen (top), and male (right)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASolenopsis.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Fire_Ant_Festival_sign%2C_Ashburn%2C_GA%2C_US.jpg/500px-Fire_Ant_Festival_sign%2C_Ashburn%2C_GA%2C_US.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Fire_Ant_Festival_sign%2C_Ashburn%2C_GA%2C_US.jpg/1280px-Fire_Ant_Festival_sign%2C_Ashburn%2C_GA%2C_US.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Fire_Ant_Festival_sign%2C_Ashburn%2C_GA%2C_US.jpg/500px-Fire_Ant_Festival_sign%2C_Ashburn%2C_GA%2C_US.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sign for the Fire Ant Festival in Ashburn, Georgia ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFire_Ant_Festival_sign%2C_Ashburn%2C_GA%2C_US.jpg"},{"srcset":"http